# Health App Monorepo

University Health App project (FERI). React web + Flutter mobile + Supabase backend + OCR service + scraper.

## Layout

```
react-app/   # React web app (Vite + React Router + OpenStreetMap)
mobile/      # Flutter app for iOS + Android
supabase/    # Supabase project config, migrations, edge functions
scraper/     # Node.js data scraper
ocr/         # (planned) OCR service
DESIGN.md    # Endurance Performance System — visual source of truth
```

Each subproject is self-contained with its own dependencies and `.gitignore`. **Do NOT** introduce `npm/pnpm workspaces`, Turborepo, or Nx unless explicitly asked.

## Tech stack

| Area    | Stack                                                              |
| ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Web     | React, Vite, OpenStreetMap                                         |
| Mobile  | Flutter 3.x, Dart 3.x, Riverpod 3, go_router, Supabase Flutter SDK |
| Backend | Supabase (Postgres + Auth + Edge Functions)                        |
| OCR     | Standalone HTTP service (to be implemented in `/ocr`)              |
| Scraper | Node.js                                                            |

## Cross-cutting rules

1. **Never commit secrets.** All `.env` files are gitignored. Use `.env.example` to document required keys.
2. **DESIGN.md is authoritative.** All UI work must respect it. Token names map 1:1 to code constants — never hardcode hex colors or pixel values. See `design-system.mdc`.
3. **No comments unless explicitly asked.** No narrating comments. Code self-documents via naming.
4. **Mock-first development.** Mobile (and web) must work end-to-end against mock sources before any real backend wiring. Source swaps are one-line DI changes.
5. **Pick latest stable versions** when adding deps. Use `flutter pub add` / `npm install` — don't hand-write version constraints.

## Checklist before changing code

1. Identify the subproject (`react-app/`, `mobile/`, `supabase/`, `scraper/`).
2. Read matching rules: `mobile-architecture.mdc` for `mobile/**`, `design-system.mdc` for any UI work.
3. Verify design-system token usage if the change is visual.
4. Run the subproject's analyzer/tests before declaring done (e.g., `flutter analyze && flutter test`).
5. Keep PRs scoped to a single concern.
